{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a good-quality, large family sized dwellinghouse. This would be detrimental to the borough&#39;s stock of these type of dwellings, the identified local need for which is set out in the Development Plan and supporting evidence.&nbsp;The provision of two smaller units is not considered sufficient to justify this, particularly noting that there would be no increase in bedrooms and the units would not provide a high quality of accommodation. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#39;s supply of&nbsp;dwellinghouses&nbsp;capable of accommodating a large family significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#39;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D6, H1, H2, H9 and&nbsp;H10 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policies SPDG 1,&nbsp;SP3 and DMH5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
